#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186486788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186174840 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aceb6eeb-1f00-5f1c-98f7-83af119247db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175692 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10584" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175692 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/bd/bdaee2dee98e41505c8a35c617a8f4fc035125ea8d504efecbe58afc9f7fd06c.png)\n\nIn the figure above,  $m \\angle CBD = 5x - 5^\\circ$ and $m \\angle ABD =2x + 10^\\circ .$ If $\\angle CBD \\cong \\angle ABD$, find $m \\angle ABC.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175692 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bea49cf1-02d0-5aa0-9584-f2ea5a2eb30c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175692 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $\\angle CBD \\cong \\angle ABD$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CBD & =m∠ABD \\\\ 5x-{5}^{∘} & =2x+{10}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & =2x+{15}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & ={15}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={5}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $\\angle CBD$ is\n\n$$\nm \\angle CBD = 5x - 5^\\circ = 5 \\cdot 5^\\circ - 5^\\circ = 20^\\circ.\n$$\n\nSo, by the angle addition postulate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ABC & =m∠CBD+m∠ABD \\\\  & =m∠CBD+m∠CBD \\\\  & =2\\cdot m∠CBD \\\\  & =2\\cdot {20}^{∘} \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175761 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2605" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175761 #edb/ref 1071 "From the information given below, find all of the angles that are congruent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={10}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠C & ={80}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠D & ={90}^{∘}-m∠C, \\\\ m∠E & =m∠B.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175761 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fbd1b514-35d8-54a1-91c1-168d330811e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175761 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the measures of $\\angle D$ and $\\angle E\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠D & ={90}^{∘}-m∠C \\\\  & ={90}^{∘}-{80}^{∘} \\\\  & ={10}^{∘} \\\\  \\\\ m∠E & =m∠B \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={10}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘} \\\\ m∠C & ={80}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={10}^{∘} \\\\ m∠E & ={40}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have that $m \\angle A = m \\angle D$ and $m \\angle B = m \\angle E.$\n\nTherefore, $\\angle A \\cong \\angle D$ and $\\angle B \\cong \\angle E.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175762 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175762 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown below?\n\nI. $\\angle AOB\t\\cong \\angle COD$\n\nII. $\\angle COD \\cong \\angle BOC$\n\nIII. $m\\angle BOC = m\\angle DOE$\n\n![](images/7d/7d0729a38dd775d0f049656b23755ace3b42d07a4040004e14942c789544c30b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175762 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bab99447-be6e-5ac0-906c-a9df9aa7f3f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175762 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $\\angle AOB$ and $\\angle COD$ are each marked with a single hash mark \"$|$,\" while\n\n- $\\angle BOC$ and $\\angle DOE$ are each marked with a double hash mark \"$||.$\"\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠COD \\\\ ∠BOC & ≅∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠COD \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176044 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186176044 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759