ref 17592186486597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487213 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "82dbe361-354a-56ad-a1e1-311213fab97b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186486727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487248 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c61077a2-9a63-5c31-b3bc-86812d3d0fa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487316 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487316 #edb/ref 1069 "q-27340" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487316 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487316 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/9c/9c14d7a4f9a460c3219cb457ff9f8ba8fb32a22101dfba3e0925aa8077b011cf.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $∠ABC$ is an angle and $D$ is a point in the interior of $∠ABC$ such that $m∠CBD=5x+{3}^{∘}.$ If $m∠ABC={106}^{∘}$ and $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, find the value of $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487316 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38145db5-f11d-5939-a57b-880dc1abb8bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487316 #edb/ref 1074 "By the angle addition postulate,\n\n$$\nm∠ABC=m∠ABD+m∠CBD.\n$$\n\nSince $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, then we have $m∠CBD=m∠ABD.$  Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ABC & =m∠ABD+m∠CBD \\\\  & =m∠CBD+m∠CBD \\\\  & =2m∠CBD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that $m∠CBD=5x+{3}^{∘}$ and $m∠ABC={106}^{∘},$ we can solve for $x$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{106}^{∘} & =2(5x+3) \\\\ {106}^{∘} & =10x+{6}^{∘} \\\\ {100}^{∘} & =10x \\\\ {10}^{∘} & =x \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487320 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487320 #edb/ref 1069 "q-103282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487320 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487320 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6f/6fe8fc042cc8d5645e9cf0df2fd297e018504c4248a45d348e4778a14caea9ca.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown above?\n\nI. $m∠AOB=m∠DOE$\n\nII. $m∠BOC=m∠COD$\n\nIII. $m∠BOC=m∠EOF$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487320 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "432febe7-1220-5082-90e3-bf3d1c64fe2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487320 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $∠AOB$ and $∠DOE$ are marked with $|$,\n\n- $∠BOC$ and $∠COD$ are marked with $||$, and\n\n- $∠EOF$ is marked with $|||.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠DOE \\\\ ∠BOC & ≅∠COD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠DOE \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠COD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo statements I and II are true, while statement III is false." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487330 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487330 #edb/ref 1069 "q-52667" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487330 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487330 #edb/ref 1071 "From the information given below, find all of the angles that are congruent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={30}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠B & ={150}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠C & ={180}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠D & ={180}^{∘}-m∠C, \\\\ m∠E & ={120}^{∘}+m∠A, \\\\ m∠F & =m∠E.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487330 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5707b071-c7c6-5712-89ca-e66cbdfb1c32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487330 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the measures of $∠D$, $∠E$ and $∠F:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠D & ={180}^{∘}-m∠C \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={0}^{∘} \\\\  \\\\ m∠E & ={120}^{∘}+m∠A \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={150}^{∘} \\\\  \\\\ m∠F & =m∠E={150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={30}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={150}^{∘} \\\\ m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={0}^{∘} \\\\ m∠E & ={150}^{∘} \\\\ m∠F & ={150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have that $m∠B=m∠E=m∠F.$ Therefore, $∠B≅∠E≅∠F.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487394 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487394 #edb/ref 1069 "q-103278" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487394 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487394 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/62/62412006e358dd798b602547e22eb63c9c274b0d740df885e9c69a1af06bcb97.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown above?\n\nI. $m∠AOB=m∠COD$\n\nII. $m∠BOC=m∠EOF$\n\nIII. $m∠COD=m∠DOE$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487394 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e51f05e0-1186-559b-935a-5d0ce775e04e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487394 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $∠AOB$ and $∠EOF$ are marked with $|$,\n\n- $∠BOC$ and $∠DOE$ are marked with $||$, and\n\n- $∠COD$ is marked with $|||.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠EOF \\\\ ∠BOC & ≅∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠EOF \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the statements listed is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487404 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487404 #edb/ref 1069 "q-103249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487404 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487404 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/cb/cb2cda27c9ca2744c059279e853969858a7b3d1882cde343177badc7aa33145d.png)\n\nWhich of the angles shown above are congruent?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487404 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fbfe98b2-d913-5b5f-9244-1e7d8b4485eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487404 #edb/ref 1074 "From the diagram, we see that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1 & ={25}^{∘} \\\\ m∠2 & ={75}^{∘} \\\\ m∠3 & ={75}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠2 & ≅∠3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
